      "writtenOn": "2023-04-05T08:21:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not 100% sure but the way I understand this, this feature controls with what `-std\u003dc++\u003cnumber\u003e` flag cxx compiles the C++ code when cxx takes care of the build in a cargo environment and thus controls what\u0027s allowed on the C++ side of the bridge declarations and definitions. \n\nI could not find any other references to `#[cfg(feature \u003d \"c++17\")]` and `#[cfg(feature \u003d \"c++21\")]` in the cxx code.\n\nI suspect we may not need this if we have our own bazel steps for compilation of the bridge code.\n\nhttps://github.com/dtolnay/cxx/blob/master/flags/src/impl.rs",
